WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.049 --> 00:00:05.436
- Hey guys this is Evan
Carmichael, my one word

00:00:05.436 --> 00:00:07.833
is believe and I believe
that all the world's

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:10.817
major problems will be
solved by entrepreneurs.

00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:13.185
So to help you on your path,
today we're going to learn

00:00:13.185 --> 00:00:17.352
nine surprising facts about
Alibaba founder, Jack Ma.

00:00:18.938 --> 00:00:21.938
(soft techno music)

00:00:30.454 --> 00:00:34.316
- Fact number one, he used
to guide tours for free

00:00:34.316 --> 00:00:39.030
in China for nine years to
learn new ways of thinking.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.787
- For nine years, every
morning, almost, whether snow,

00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:45.686
rain or sun, I went there
looking for foreign tourists

00:00:45.686 --> 00:00:47.377
to become the free guide.

00:00:47.377 --> 00:00:48.791
And I made a lot of friends.

00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:52.492
This trained me the way
of think different from

00:00:52.492 --> 00:00:55.075
the other kids in China, my generation.

00:00:55.075 --> 00:00:58.742
'Cuz everything I learned
from the tourists,

00:00:59.633 --> 00:01:01.071
foreign tourists are so different

00:01:01.071 --> 00:01:05.174
from the things I
learned from the schools,

00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:08.188
my parents because we
thought China was like that,

00:01:08.188 --> 00:01:10.607
the world was like that, in our books.

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:13.682
But the thing that I learned from outside

00:01:13.682 --> 00:01:15.038
they are so different.

00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:18.538
So that trained my way
of thinking different.

00:01:18.538 --> 00:01:20.602
When people talk about everything,

00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:22.571
when everything people agree,

00:01:22.571 --> 00:01:26.345
normally I take one minute
to think about is that true?

00:01:26.345 --> 00:01:29.068
When everything disagree, I
say take about a one minute,

00:01:29.068 --> 00:01:31.740
think about it, hmm, is that true?

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.657
So that was a training.

00:01:34.935 --> 00:01:38.757
- Fact number two, his
hero is Forrest Gump.

00:01:38.757 --> 00:01:41.507
- The hero I had is Forrest Gump.

00:01:42.347 --> 00:01:44.030
Fourteen years ago when,

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:45.517
- Want some chocolates?
- Yeah.

00:01:45.517 --> 00:01:47.194
- You know he's a
fictional character though.

00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:49.837
- I really like that guy,
I've been watching that movie

00:01:49.837 --> 00:01:51.432
for about 10 times.

00:01:51.432 --> 00:01:54.293
Every time when I'm
frustrated, I watch the movie.

00:01:54.293 --> 00:01:56.883
And I watch movie before
I came here, again.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.965
- [Co-host] What are you doing?

00:01:57.965 --> 00:01:59.945
- Yeah, for coming to the New York,

00:01:59.945 --> 00:02:02.291
because I watch the movie again,

00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:05.207
and telling me that, no
matter whatever changed,

00:02:05.207 --> 00:02:08.502
you are you, and I'm still the guy,

00:02:08.502 --> 00:02:12.085
15 years ago, I only
earn like $20 a month.

00:02:13.397 --> 00:02:16.647
And today I can do that much, you know.

00:02:17.621 --> 00:02:20.892
- Fact number three, he has
no technical background,

00:02:20.892 --> 00:02:23.202
started with one dollar in his pocket,

00:02:23.202 --> 00:02:24.988
and beer was the first thing

00:02:24.988 --> 00:02:27.083
that he searched on the internet.

00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:31.096
- And when I go to register
company called, internet,

00:02:31.096 --> 00:02:33.669
the registry office said
no, there's no such word,

00:02:33.669 --> 00:02:34.915
internet in the dictionary,

00:02:34.915 --> 00:02:36.901
how can you register an internet.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.855
So they say, you have to
register another name,

00:02:38.855 --> 00:02:40.815
I said what's the name?

00:02:40.815 --> 00:02:43.653
He said, Computer Consulting Firm.

00:02:43.653 --> 00:02:46.285
And I have no idea about what is computer.

00:02:46.285 --> 00:02:47.675
So my first company,

00:02:47.675 --> 00:02:50.925
Hangzhou Hope Computer Consulting Firm.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.708
It was tough, without knowing
anything about technolog,

00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:59.321
without knowing anything about computer,

00:02:59.321 --> 00:03:02.392
in the past 15 years, I've been working.

00:03:02.392 --> 00:03:04.319
I call myself like a blind man,

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:06.557
riding on the back of the blind tigers.

00:03:06.557 --> 00:03:07.748
(audience laughing)

00:03:07.748 --> 00:03:10.976
Those experts riding
horses, they all fell.

00:03:10.976 --> 00:03:14.027
We survived because we
worry about the future.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.381
We believe the future, we change ourself,

00:03:16.381 --> 00:03:18.714
we never compete the others.

00:04:25.621 --> 00:04:27.820
- Fact number four, is life is full

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.643
of failures and rejections.

00:04:30.643 --> 00:04:34.216
- Tried to get into three colleges.

00:04:34.216 --> 00:04:36.506
Each time they rejected you.

00:04:36.506 --> 00:04:40.147
- No, I tried, there's a
examination, that young people,

00:04:40.147 --> 00:04:41.401
if you want to go university you have

00:04:41.401 --> 00:04:43.725
to take the examination.

00:04:43.725 --> 00:04:45.233
So I failed it three times.

00:04:45.233 --> 00:04:46.182
But I have a lot of fail.

00:04:46.182 --> 00:04:48.765
I fail for funny things that I failed

00:04:48.765 --> 00:04:52.448
a key primary school test for two times,

00:04:52.448 --> 00:04:56.531
and I failed, three times
for the middle schools.

00:05:00.517 --> 00:05:03.845
You would never believe,
in Hangzhou, my city,

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:06.428
there's only one middle school,

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.434
that last only one year.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.243
It was change from primary
school to middle school,

00:05:12.243 --> 00:05:15.599
because I want our
graduates of our school,

00:05:15.599 --> 00:05:19.766
no middle school accept us,
because we were too bad.

00:05:21.319 --> 00:05:23.646
So we become a middle school.

00:05:23.646 --> 00:05:26.479
When I graduate from universities,

00:05:27.477 --> 00:05:29.265
and before, for three years,

00:05:29.265 --> 00:05:31.172
I tried and failed in the universities,

00:05:31.172 --> 00:05:34.589
so apply jobs for 30 times, got rejected.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.112
I went for a police, they
said, "no you're not good."

00:05:39.112 --> 00:05:42.822
I went to even the KFC,
when KFC come to China,

00:05:42.822 --> 00:05:45.677
come to my city,
- [Host] You applied.

00:05:45.677 --> 00:05:47.927
24 people went for the job,

00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:53.537
23 people accepted, I
was the only one guy.

00:05:53.537 --> 00:05:56.039
And we went for police, 5 people,

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:59.799
4 of them accepted, I was
the only guy that receive it.

00:05:59.799 --> 00:06:02.991
So to me, being turned down, rejected,

00:06:02.991 --> 00:06:06.415
oh by the way, I told you
that I apply for Harvard,

00:06:06.415 --> 00:06:08.947
for 10 times rejected.
(audience laughs)

00:06:08.947 --> 00:06:10.464
I know they reject, I just want to see ...

00:06:10.464 --> 00:06:12.131
- They're sorry now.

00:06:13.677 --> 00:06:15.150
Ten times you wrote them and said,

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.846
"I'd like to come to Harvard."

00:06:16.846 --> 00:06:18.703
- Yeah. And then I told myself,

00:06:18.703 --> 00:06:20.319
someday I should go teach there probably.

00:06:20.319 --> 00:06:23.413
(audience laughing)

00:06:23.413 --> 00:06:26.210
- Fact number five, he
chose the name Alibaba,

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.203
because he liked the open sesame story.

00:06:29.203 --> 00:06:32.534
- Why did you call the company Alibaba?

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:35.019
- I like the spelling
and I like the vision,

00:06:35.019 --> 00:06:36.571
Ali Baba open sesame.

00:06:36.571 --> 00:06:40.022
I believe the internet is open sesame,

00:06:40.022 --> 00:06:42.403
and there is pass world to everybody,

00:06:42.403 --> 00:06:44.528
that you can find the great people,

00:06:44.528 --> 00:06:48.874
you can find a great
opportunities of business,

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:53.266
and improve people, that
is open sesame story.

00:06:53.266 --> 00:06:57.325
I love the Alibaba, it saves
me a lot of marketing dollars.

00:06:57.325 --> 00:06:59.900
When I started, I think,
Internet is global,

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.913
we should have global name.

00:07:01.913 --> 00:07:05.059
And a name that, interesting like,

00:07:05.059 --> 00:07:08.059
at that time the best name is Yahoo.

00:07:09.144 --> 00:07:10.700
So I been thinking for many days,

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.453
suddenly thinking, Alibaba is good name.

00:07:12.453 --> 00:07:16.342
So I was happen to be in
San Francisco that day.

00:07:16.342 --> 00:07:19.463
I have a lunch, and the waitress come.

00:07:19.463 --> 00:07:21.479
I ask her, do you know about Ali Baba?

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:23.767
She say, "Yes", I say,
"What is Ali Baba?",

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:25.703
she say, "Open sesame."

00:07:25.703 --> 00:07:26.804
Good.

00:07:26.804 --> 00:07:30.317
So I went down the street,
I ask about 10, 20 people.

00:07:30.317 --> 00:07:33.172
They all know about Ali
Baba, forty thieves,

00:07:33.172 --> 00:07:37.808
and open sesame, and I
think, this is a good name.

00:07:37.808 --> 00:07:40.171
Start with A, what ever you talk about,

00:07:40.171 --> 00:07:42.004
Alibaba is always top.

00:07:44.366 --> 00:07:47.480
- Fact number six, he learned
English by watching TV,

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.329
because there were no other
options in China at the time.

00:07:50.329 --> 00:07:53.435
- Think, there is no way to
learn English at that time.

00:07:53.435 --> 00:07:55.166
There's no teachers in our city,

00:07:55.166 --> 00:07:58.018
who can teach people to speak English.

00:07:58.018 --> 00:08:02.058
So I listen to the BBC
and Voice of America.

00:08:02.058 --> 00:08:05.706
And there, every evening, nine o'clock,

00:08:05.706 --> 00:08:10.147
eight o'clock to nine
o'clock, I open my video,

00:08:10.147 --> 00:08:14.065
Monday, Wednesday, and
Friday, I listen to the VOA,

00:08:14.065 --> 00:08:18.232
the first book I heard about
is the Adventure of Tom Sawyer.

00:08:20.187 --> 00:08:21.445
- Fact number seven.

00:08:21.445 --> 00:08:25.112
He performs mass weddings
for his employees.

00:08:39.086 --> 00:08:41.260
(upbeat music)

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:44.927
(speaking foreign language)

00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:08.485
- Fact number eight, he
wants to retire early,

00:10:08.485 --> 00:10:12.075
explore other interests,
and die on a beach.

00:10:12.075 --> 00:10:16.123
- People say this is a uncertain world.

00:10:16.123 --> 00:10:20.605
Every day's uncertain, the
only certain day was yesterday.

00:10:20.605 --> 00:10:23.558
I'm not sure about that in the future,

00:10:23.558 --> 00:10:26.098
I will dictate, I will be stupid,

00:10:26.098 --> 00:10:29.900
that's why I should retire
early, when I'm young.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.807
That is why I have a lot
of things that I dream

00:10:31.807 --> 00:10:33.583
I want to do, I want to do philanthropy,

00:10:33.583 --> 00:10:35.901
I want to be a teacher, I
want to go back to school,

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:37.613
I want to do the environment.

00:10:37.613 --> 00:10:39.295
And the world is so wonderful,

00:10:39.295 --> 00:10:42.801
why should it be the sea
of Alibaba all the time?

00:10:42.801 --> 00:10:46.253
I'm come in to this world not to work.

00:10:46.253 --> 00:10:48.446
I want to come to this
world to enjoy my life.

00:10:48.446 --> 00:10:49.738
I don't want to die in my office,

00:10:49.738 --> 00:10:52.155
I want to die on the beaches.

00:10:53.993 --> 00:10:56.509
- Fact number nine, he
once dressed up and sang

00:10:56.509 --> 00:11:00.009
the Lion King theme song to his employees.

00:11:01.052 --> 00:11:02.237
- [Narrator] I'd worked
as a vice-president

00:11:02.237 --> 00:11:04.635
in his company for nearly ten years.

00:11:04.635 --> 00:11:06.700
As our team survived the Internet bubble,

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:10.133
fought a war with Ebay, and
managed to build China's first

00:11:10.133 --> 00:11:12.438
global internet company,

00:11:12.438 --> 00:11:14.705
I settled into my seat and wondered,

00:11:14.705 --> 00:11:18.187
how would Jack address us
on this important night?

00:11:18.187 --> 00:11:20.546
And then, just like any other billionaire

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:23.326
in the same situation,
Jack took the stage.

00:11:23.326 --> 00:11:27.243
(singing in foreign language)

00:11:34.587 --> 00:11:38.587
♫ Can you feel the love tonight

00:11:42.895 --> 00:11:44.693
- [Narrator] Well, it
may not have been typical

00:11:44.693 --> 00:11:46.126
for a company chairman,

00:11:46.126 --> 00:11:49.073
but it wasn't surprising coming from Jack.

00:11:49.073 --> 00:11:51.730
People outside the company
assumed he was crazy,

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.407
but those of us inside
the company knew better.

00:11:54.407 --> 00:11:55.308
- So guys, thank you so much for watching,

00:11:55.308 --> 00:11:56.701
I hope you enjoyed.

00:11:56.701 --> 00:11:59.005
I'd love to know what was
the most surprising fact

00:11:59.005 --> 00:12:01.837
that you learned about
Jack Ma in this video,

00:12:01.837 --> 00:12:03.206
leave it in the comments below,

00:12:03.206 --> 00:12:04.828
really curious to see
what you have to say.

00:12:04.828 --> 00:12:06.022
Thank you so much for watching,

00:12:06.022 --> 00:12:07.156
I believe in you.

00:12:07.156 --> 00:12:09.221
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:12:09.221 --> 00:12:11.196
and whatever your one word is,

00:12:11.196 --> 00:12:12.618
much love.

00:12:12.618 --> 00:12:14.035
I'll see ya soon.

